Installation instructions for the SAM suite.

Binary wheel installation (recommended)
---------------------------------------

Create a virtual environment and install the wheel for your operating system
and architecture:

    python -m venv .venv
    . .venv/bin/activate
    python -m pip install samsrcv5

On Windows, activate with `.venv\Scripts\activate`. A wheel installation does
not require Make, a compiler, GSL, or FFTW. Until artifacts are published to
PyPI, give pip the downloaded `.whl` filename instead of `samsrcv5`.

AFNI, FreeSurfer, and qhull are external applications and are not distributed
in the wheel. ROIbuilder also requires a system GTK3/PyGObject installation.

Source installation
-------------------

Source builds require CMake, Ninja or Make, a C17 compiler, GSL development
files, and FFTW3 development files. If GSL and FFTW share a non-standard
prefix, set `SAM_DEPS_ROOT` before installing:

    SAM_DEPS_ROOT=/path/to/deps python -m pip install .

Wheel maintainers can build pinned static GSL 2.8 and FFTW 3.3.11 copies with:

    SAM_DEPS_CACHE=/path/to/cache \
    SAM_DEPS_PREFIX=/path/to/prefix \
        tools/build_native_deps.sh

Legacy Make installation
------------------------

The original Unix build remains available. Install GSL and FFTW development
packages, review `config/Makefile.config` and optional `config/Makefile.site`,
then run `make`. Executables are written to `bin/` and libraries to `lib/`.
